Comment=This Hypothesis has been proven by JL by writing and loading this WDR file�=========��This example is there to demo what happens when there are INI file comment chars ';' in the middle of text.�Ideally it will be escaped somehow so it can be round tripped in the text.��We suspect that WinIsd adheres to Windows INI conventions ... "Under Windows, the Profile API is the programming interface used to read and write settings from classic Windows .ini "��This page shows which features windows supports. �Init file escape chars - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/INI_file�See the comment section ...�   var = a       ; This is an inline comment�   foo = bar     # This is another inline comment�   hello;there#again��but also ...�   Under the WinAPI's GetPrivateProfileString's dialect, comments must occur on lines by themselves.��So its likely that the semicolons on this page will NOT be regarded as comments if WinIsd repects GetPrivateProfileString's ��This file tests this hypothesis.�[ENV T=283.15 p=161325 RH=35]
